                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 17 at 3:18PM MDT until September 17 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "FFWABQ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Albuquerque has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Salt burn scar in...\nSouth Central Lincoln County in central New Mexico...\n\n* Until 430 PM MDT.\n\n* At 318 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over and downstream of the Salt Burn Scar. Between 1.5\nand 2.5 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of\n0.5 to 1 inch are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is\nalready occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Salt Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nSalt Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nRuidoso Downs and Glencoe.",
                "instruction": "This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks, streams and ditches in\nthe Salt Burn Scar. Severe debris flows can also be anticipated\nacross roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in places. If\nyou encounter flood waters, climb to safety.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
